## Cohesion Check Complete: Travis-Kelce.md

**Before score: 8.5/10**
**After score: 9/10**

### Central Thesis

Travis Kelce is a Type 7 whose appetite nearly destroyed his career and whose greatness runs on discipline he openly admits other people installed; the test of his life is whether a man built around exits can stay in one room.

### Thread Map

1. **Cold open (car keys)** → plants the appetite at age three and states the thesis promise: the discipline "was not his."
2. **Diagnosis** → names Type 7, shows the bright side (momentum, full send), then the shadow: pain metabolized into a bit, which hands off directly to...
3. **Cincinnati** → the appetite's paper trail; Jason saves him; punishment reframed into gratitude. Ends on the Butch Jones jersey.
4. **No. 87** → opens on that exact jersey ("He pays Jason back every Sunday"), goes back to childhood to explain the debt. The number is a receipt.
5. **The Discipline That Isn't His** → extends not-self-made from Jason to Reid/Veach; the one arena where the Seven went deep.
6. **The Super Bowl shove** → what happens when the reframe machinery has nothing to work on; the stress pattern, resolved inside the section with the OT win.
7. **Can't Do Just One Thing** → the appetite at full stretch in 2025; the cost; "I'm not going out like this" sets up the 14th season.
8. **The Bracelet** → "the biggest yes of his life" carries the yes-to-everything keyword into the Swift arc; ends "even the altar was an arena."
9. **The Only Room He Won't Leave** → resolves both threads: the man built around exits stayed (discipline thread) and now faces the one exit he can't reframe (appetite thread).

The chain reads coherently top to bottom. Every section serves the thesis; removing any of 3–6 would collapse the argument.

